#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:878
msgid "even games · random, no repeat"
msgstr "势均力敌 · 随机、不重复"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1145
msgid "every round a real ILP solve"
msgstr "每一轮都是真实的整数线性规划求解"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:980
msgid "For a single court of five or six players, the rating system admittedly adds little. The tool still helps: it remembers who has partnered whom, keeps play counts even, and tracks each player's rating change round by round even with nothing submitted — the session runs fairly, and everyone sees how they actually did. People reliably overrate their own performance, even when they do not show it."
msgstr "对于只有五六名球员的单场地活动，评分系统确实作用不大。但这个工具仍然有用：它记得谁和谁搭过档，让上场次数保持平均，并逐轮跟踪每位球员的评分变化，即使什么都不提交——活动运行得公平，每个人都能看到自己的真实表现。人们总会高估自己的表现，即便嘴上不说。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1002
msgid "Future improvements"
msgstr "未来的改进"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:698
msgid "How the numbers were made: one simulation — 24 players, 4 courts, 100 rounds — replayed across 7 seeds in three synthetic clubs: varied (skills spread across the range, plus a ringer and a beginner), typical (about a 1.0 DUPR spread), and tight (a bunched pack). True skills are not frozen: as in a real club, about 20% of players improve gradually, one improves quickly — up to half a DUPR point, with gains tapering as they settle — and one slowly slips, the same players in every strategy's run so the comparison stays fair. Every round is a real solve through the same optimiser the app uses. Charts are 5-round rolling averages across all seeds; headline numbers summarise the last 25 rounds. Timescales: a real session is 12–14 rounds, so round 13 stands in for “one session” below, while the 100-round horizon — seven or eight sessions of persisted ratings — shows the system once everyone's rating is mature. Charts are interactive — hover for values, click a strategy to isolate its line."
msgstr "数据是如何得出的：一次模拟——24 名球员、4 片球场、100 轮——在三个合成俱乐部中各用 7 个随机种子重放：差异大（技术水平分布很广，还有一名高手和一名新手）、典型（DUPR 跨度约 1.0）和紧密（水平非常集中）。真实水平并非固定不变：与真实俱乐部一样，约 20% 的球员会逐步进步，一人进步很快——最多提升半个 DUPR 点，随着水平稳定增幅逐渐放缓——还有一人慢慢退步；每种策略的运行中都是同一批球员，以保证比较公平。每一轮都由应用所用的同一优化器真实求解。图表为所有种子上的 5 轮滚动平均；关键数字汇总最后 25 轮。时间尺度：一场真实活动约 12–14 轮，因此下文用第 13 轮代表“一场活动”，而 100 轮的跨度——七八场活动的累积评分——展示的是所有人评分成熟后的系统表现。图表可交互——悬停查看数值，点击某个策略可单独显示其曲线。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:983
msgid "If you are going to use a round robin table at all, use the Pkuru Round Robin tool: the same table, better matches, every default tunable. And every simulation in this article can be rerun for a club shaped like yours."
msgstr "如果你打算使用循环赛对阵表，就用 Pkuru 循环赛工具：同样的表格，更好的对阵，所有默认设置都可调。本文中的每个模拟都可以按你的俱乐部情况重新运行。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:761
msgid "In a tight club even the static Competitive+ profile keeps up with Balanced Round Robin almost immediately: when everyone is close, a band drawn from noisy ratings is barely different from one drawn from true skill, so banding costs nothing here. The adaptive Competitive+ tracks Balanced Round Robin from the first round by construction — it runs it until ratings settle. The calibration phase earns its keep in the wider clubs below, where banding on noise genuinely restricts the movement that would fix the ratings."
msgstr "在紧密型俱乐部中，即使是静态的 Competitive+ 配置也几乎立刻就能跟上平衡循环赛：当所有人水平接近时，用带噪声的评分划分的分组与按真实水平划分几乎没有差别，因此分组在这里没有代价。自适应 Competitive+ 从第一轮起就与平衡循环赛一致——这是设计使然，它会先运行平衡循环赛直到评分稳定。校准阶段真正发挥作用的是下面差异更大的俱乐部，那里基于噪声的分组会实质性地限制本可修正评分的流动性。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:773
msgid "In the real world assembling a tight club of similarly skilled players is challenging because on any given day a player's performance might fluctuate by 0.5 points or more. The rating system however can adjust for this variance within a few rounds of play."
msgstr "在现实中，组建一个水平相近的紧密型俱乐部很有难度，因为在任何一天，球员的表现都可能波动 0.5 分甚至更多。不过评分系统能在几轮比赛内适应这种波动。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:684
msgid "Inversion"
msgstr "倒置"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:826
msgid "JP-style open play is the avoid-repeats baseline plus one intervention: a foursome is split when it is obviously lopsided — the pairs half a DUPR apart, the bar real organisers actually use. The surprise is that the intervention buys nothing measurable: JP lands within the error bars of its own baseline everywhere, a point or two of quality in this club at best. Splits that rare cannot move a session. Politeness that fixes only the egregious matches is worth almost nothing; the gains begin when every match is deliberately balanced, which is exactly what nobody does socially."
msgstr "日式开放打法是“避免重复”基线加上一项干预：当一组四人明显失衡时将其拆开——两对相差半个 DUPR，这正是真实组织者使用的标准。令人意外的是，这项干预没带来任何可测量的收益：日式打法在各处都落在其自身基线的误差范围内，在这个俱乐部里最多提升一两点质量。如此少见的拆分无法改变一场活动。只修正最离谱对阵的“客气”几乎毫无价值；收益要等到每一场对阵都被刻意平衡时才会出现，而这恰恰是社交场合中没人会做的事。"

